      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would break avatars that utilize the old naming scheme, so it probably won't be done. They could switch now and support older avatars (like they did fallbacks) while providing notice for the new parameter names, but that adds complexity to the client and devs.\nI do agree though any new parameters should be prefixed. It needs to be obvious a parameter is built-in for new learners too.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-03-11T07:46:44.780Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Please heavily consider the use of prefixing animation parameters such as \"Voice\" with \"VRCVoice\" and creating documentation warning that parameters prefixed by \"VRC\" may break in the future.\nThis is in order to prevent situations in the future where a newly reserved parameter used previously by a creator inadvertently causes avatars to fail to initialize.",
